{% macro ship_shape(stack) %}
## What this cycle ships

{% if stack %}
The cycle ships one commit per PR of the design's **Stack** section, in
stack order, each on its own branch. The designer decides the split, and nothing ships
outside it: no PR the section does not name, no second commit inside a PR,
no other order. A request or design that dictates a different commit shape
specifies something this workflow will not produce.
{% else %}
The whole cycle lands as **one commit** on the launch branch: every round
is squashed, and the ship gate squashes all rounds into one. No
intermediate commit, branch or ordering survives. A request or design that
specifies several commits, separate PRs or a particular commit sequence
specifies something this workflow cannot produce. Another workflow ships
work as several reviewable commits; this is not it.
{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
